#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
genesi-automationd — Genesi AI Mode Monitor automation engine (per-user daemon).

This is the background half of the Monitor's "Automations" tab: an n8n-style,
PC-wide automation runner. The GUI only EDITS automations (a node/link graph, the
same shape as the Forge Canvas); this daemon is what actually runs them, idle in
the background, whether or not the Monitor window is open. It is a systemd --user
service so it comes up in every Genesi session (Plasma, Hyprland, GNOME, Xfce,
Cinnamon, Budgie, LXDE, Cosmic, Niri) and even on a "No Desktop" install.

Contract with the GUI (genesi_ai_monitor.py Backend):
    ~/.config/genesi-ai-monitor/automations/<id>.json   one automation each
        { id, name, enabled, mode?, nodes[], links[] }   (GUI writes, we watch)
    ~/.local/state/genesi-automation/status.json         run state + logs (we write)
    $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/genesi-automationd.sock             control socket (reload /
        run-now / capture-hotkey / ping)

Event nodes (triggers), each with config.mode = "once" | "always":
    evt_fs        a path: file/folder created / modified / deleted (inotify)
    evt_resource  cpu% or ram% crosses a threshold (psutil, edge-triggered)
    evt_app       a process name opens / closes (psutil)
    evt_hotkey    a global key or key-combo (evdev; needs the 'input' group)
    evt_schedule  every N minutes, a HH:MM time of day, or a cron expression
    evt_clipboard something new was copied (polled; no display-server dep)
    evt_screenshot a new image landed in the screenshots folder
    evt_webhook   an HTTP call to a local endpoint (loopback unless a token is set)
    evt_manual     fired only by the GUI's "Run now"

Action nodes:
    act_script    run a shell command / script
    act_ai        drive local AI: pick model, optionally AI Mode + Turbo (on the
                  chosen model), optionally let it act autonomously; run a prompt.
                  Declared `outputs` publish named values for later blocks.
    act_cond      a branch: True/False ports, by expression or by asking the model
    act_loop      repeat the `each` branch per item; `done` continues after
    act_subflow   run another automation as one step of this one
    act_email     send over SMTP / read over IMAP (password from the keyring)
    act_notify    desktop notification (notify-send)

Values between blocks:
    {input}   the previous block's whole output (unchanged, still works)
    {{name}}  a NAMED value published earlier in the run — by an AI block's
              declared outputs, by a loop ({{item}}, {{index}}, {{count}}) or by
              the email reader ({{mail_subject}}, …). An unknown name renders as
              itself, so a wiring mistake is visible instead of silently blank.

Reuses genesi_agent (tool layer) and genesi_turbo_ctl (shared Turbo control).
Stdlib only besides psutil; inotify + evdev are done with ctypes/struct so there
is no compiled dependency and it stays DE- and display-server-agnostic.
"""

